# Installed to /etc/sudoers.d/docker-daemon (mode 0440, root:root).
# Jellyfin-gated Docker lifecycle: the "Jellyfin Server" launcher starts the daemon
# on demand, and the "Stop Jellyfin" launcher tears the whole stack down. Both run
# as ethan from a Terminal launcher; NOPASSWD keeps them one click, scoped to exactly
# these fixed invocations, nothing else. `start docker.service` pulls docker.socket +
# containerd up via its unit deps; the stop takes all three back down (Wants= does not
# stop containerd, so it is listed explicitly). See my-system: services/docker.md and
# users-and-permissions/sudo-policy.md.
ethan ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl start docker.service
ethan ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl stop docker.service docker.socket containerd.service
